{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\,{v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,uv⟩$ at the point where $u=0$ and $v=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=0$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(0,2) & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(0,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(2),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(0,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(0,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,2,\\,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=0$ and $v=2$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(0)+2,\\,{2}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,0\\cdot 2)=(2,4,0),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-8,\\,2,\\,7⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-4,\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-8)\\cdot (x-2)+2\\cdot (y-4)+7\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -8x+2y+7z+8 & =0 \\\\ 8x-2y-7z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64dea7199402b5177dd473750ed2981519841ee2114d881d834e5679724dc129"} {"question" "q-109713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x-8y+3z=4"] ["math" "4x-y-6z=2"] ["math" "8x-2y-7z=8"] ["math" "8x-y+2z=6"] ["math" "x-y-z=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8x-2y-7z=8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ at the point where $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-2\\sqrt{3},\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=(1,\\sqrt{3},0),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,-2\\sqrt{3},\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-\\sqrt{3},\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-1)-2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (y-\\sqrt{3})+0\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -2x-2\\sqrt{3\\,}y+8 & =0 \\\\ -x-\\sqrt{3}\\,y+4 & =0 \\\\ x+\\sqrt{3}\\,y & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64dea7199402b5177dd473750ed2981519841ee2114d881d834e5679724dc129"} {"question" "q-109764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}\\,x-y+z=4"] ["math" "2x-\\sqrt{3}\\,y+z=8"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\,x+2z=1"] ["math" "x+2\\sqrt{3}\\,y=6"] ["math" "x+\\sqrt{3}\\,y=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109764" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+\\sqrt{3}\\,y=4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,y=-v,\\,z=-u\n$$\n\nat the point $(-1,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,-v,\\,-u⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(-1,-1,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}=-1 \\\\ -v=-1 \\\\ -u=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=-1 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=-1$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(-1,1) & =⟨-2(-1),\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(-1,1) & =⟨-2(1),\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(-1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(-1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (x+1)+2\\cdot (y+1)+(-2)\\cdot (z-1) & =0 \\\\ -x+2y-2z+3 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+2z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64dea7199402b5177dd473750ed2981519841ee2114d881d834e5679724dc129"} {"question" "q-109814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x-2y+z=-3"] ["math" "2x-y+3z=1"] ["math" "3x-2y+z=3"] ["math" "x-2y+2z=3"] ["math" "x-3y+z=-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109814" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2y+2z=3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=2{u}^{3},\\,y=u{v}^{2},\\,z=v\n$$\n\nat the point $(2,9,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2{u}^{3},\\,u{v}^{2},\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(2,9,3)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{u}^{3}=2 \\\\ u{v}^{2}=9 \\\\ v=3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2uv,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨6(1)^{2},\\,{3}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,9,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨0,\\,2(1)(3),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,3)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,\\,-6,\\,36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨9,\\,-6,\\,36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-9,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot (x-2)+(-6)\\cdot (y-9)+36\\cdot (z-3) & =0 \\\\ 9x-6y+36z-72 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+12z & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64dea7199402b5177dd473750ed2981519841ee2114d881d834e5679724dc129"} {"question" "q-109824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x-2y+12z=24"] ["math" "3x-2y-6z=-12"] ["math" "3x-y-3z=12"] ["math" "x+y-4z=12"] ["math" "x-2y-6z=24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-109824" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x-2y+12z=24"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-110067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨v,\\,1+u,\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩$ at the point $(1,2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-110067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $(1,2,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}v=1 \\\\ 1+u=2 \\\\ {u}^{2}{v}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2u{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2{u}^{2}v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2(1)(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(1)^{2}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-110067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64dea7199402b5177dd473750ed2981519841ee2114d881d834e5679724dc129"} {"question" "q-110067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070071/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7005ed03cd7226982c534437b53c4c5548b8400cd7e75fde05105e2010edb09"} {"question" "q-110067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,-1,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,0,\\,1⟩"] ["ma